  "notes": "Every ordinary-bracket threshold and rate for every filing status, tax year 2025, transcribed from the archived revenue procedure at the locator above. This file is an INPUT to the uprating fixtures and the rate-schedule grids, not a promotable tier-1 fixture: it has no corresponding id in TESTING.md section 3.1's matrix. qss has no table of its own anywhere in 26 USC 1(j)(2) or in either revenue procedure; 1(j)(2)(A) is headed 'Married Individuals Filing Joint Returns and Surviving Spouses', so qss duplicates the mfj column. Estates and trusts (1(j)(2)(E), Table 5) are not a FilingStatus and are deliberately not transcribed. The printed cumulative-tax column is carried so a reader can re-run the internal-consistency check: for all 8 tables each row's cumulative tax equals the previous row's plus the previous rate times the bracket width, in exact decimal (8 of 8 consistent)."
